# Everything the build does not need, kept out of the context.
#
# Two reasons beyond speed: node_modules from a Windows host would be copied in
# and then shadow the Linux install (native bindings for the wrong platform),
# and .env files must never be baked into an image layer, where they survive
# every later deletion and travel with the image.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
dist
**/dist
bin

# Secrets. Nothing here is copied deliberately; this is the second line.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Reference checkouts — read-only copies of other systems, never built.
Reference

# Nothing in the image reads these.
docs
design-system
.claude
.sparstrowgen
*.md
LICENSE
Makefile
scripts

# Local tooling and editor state.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Go build and test artefacts.
**/*.exe
**/*.exe~
**/*.test
